WEBVTT

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.480
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.650
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:34.070
Polar Bear's Insomnia.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:40.910
Oh, pardon me.

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:43.770
You're yawning? That's unusual.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.160
I've been suffering 
from insomnia lately.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.830
It's rough. I've been 
going through it, too.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.760
You say that, but didn't you fall asleep

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:57.720
while eating at the 
counter the other day?

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:04.740
Oh, please. I was just blinking.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:06.680
No, your eyes were completely shut.

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:10.150
They were shut, but only for a moment.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.300
Even when I close them
 for a second at night,

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.360
it becomes morning instantly.

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:18.710
You're sleeping very well.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:23.040
Are you having that much trouble 
sleeping, Polar Bear?

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.790
I tried various ways to fall asleep...

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.160
Are you taking baths every day?

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:30.580
They should help you relax.

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:34.170
I do. I take very cold ice baths.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.300
And those don't help?

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.580
Nope.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.210
You should count cute things.

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:41.880
Cute things?

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.180
If you count something as cute as me,

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:46.760
you'll feel all warm and fuzzy and get sleepy.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:50.990
One panda.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:53.310
Two pandas.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.940
Three pandas...

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:01.890
Panda is quite amazing.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:04.160
Let's wake up now, Panda.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:06.960
I'll give it a try tonight.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:15.680
It didn't work?

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.880
Are you sure you counted me correctly?

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:20.210
I did, but it didn't help.

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:22.060
That's weird.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.310
I tried counting other things, too.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:26.470
Like what?

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.220
One natto bean.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:34.050
Two natto beans.

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:36.420
That'd be a little hard to count.

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:37.990
And then...

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:39.400
What else?

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:42.160
A ship in a bottle.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:43.640
Why is there a sushi boat?

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.370
I mean, it looks good and all, but...

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:48.410
Working on intricate 
things makes you tired,

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:50.010
so I thought it'd help me sleep.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.880
But that'd make you more 
alert, wouldn't it?

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:55.380
Yeah, I ended up wide awake instead.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.710
There's someone we 
associate with sleep.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:06.960
Hello?

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:10.000
A way to fall asleep?

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.190
How the hell should I know?! 
I'm hibernating over here!

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:16.100
He got mad at me.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:18.050
Yeah, I don't blame him.

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:20.470
That was rude, Polar Bear.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:25.390
Hello?

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:28.980
Mr. Grizzly? Sorry.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.410
Have you been sleeping well?

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.560
Here!

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:37.830
The memory foam pillow you 
guys got me works well,

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:39.500
so I got you one!

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.710
Thanks.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.380
That's not all.

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:47.430
To be able to fall asleep 
immediately, scent is important.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:49.140
Lavender!

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:52.350
And then there's the flickering 
flame to calm your heart...

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:54.560
An aroma candle.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.770
And finally, a lullaby 
to play by your pillow.

00:04:58.180 --> 00:04:59.730
A music box!

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.190
What kind of ritual is this?!

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:08.330
Where do you get this 
stuff, Mr. Grizzly?

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:11.620
You're surprisingly girly, aren't you?

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:13.620
C-Can it!

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:17.580
Use all that, Polar Bear! 
You'll be able to sleep!

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.190
All right. Got it.

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:37.190
I guess it didn't work.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.710
Did you listen to the music box?

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:40.900
Yeah.

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:44.930
Damn it! I've failed.

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:46.360
Sorry.

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:49.400
They say it's not a good idea to

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.080
force yourself to sleep, either.

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:52.980
What do you mean?

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:57.120
They say that if you can't sleep, 
then you should just let it be.

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:00.330
Really?

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:05.880
It's true!

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:09.080
Thinking that I don't have
 to work if I don't feel like it

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:11.090
is really calming!

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:14.010
I think you should try working 
a little harder, actually.

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:18.570
They say it can be easier
 to sleep with a bit of white noise

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:20.620
rather than having it completely quiet.

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:24.020
So that's why I fall asleep 
when I'm at work.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:26.070
That happens everywhere for you.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:31.920
The sounds from the visitors 
talking is really soothing.

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:36.990
Polar Bear! You should 
sleep at the zoo!

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.040
There aren't any visitors at night.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:43.000
So he should come during 
the day and sleep.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:48.880
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:05.570
Hi, there...

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:09.170
Hello...

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:12.920
When I thought of something 
that makes you sleepy,

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:14.800
I thought of these two, 
so I called them over...

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:15.760
Two days ago.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:17.870
It took us...

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.660
...two days...

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:23.000
That's it. You're doing great.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.190
Getting sleepy already.

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:26.630
Really...?

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:31.950
That was too fast, Panda!

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:36.210
Huh? Did I blink again?

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:37.810
I think it's working.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:39.850
Please try talking more.

00:07:40.470 --> 00:07:43.470
You say that, but...

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:46.030
...we can't think of...

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:48.020
...what to say...

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:51.830
...so quickly...

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:55.000
I-It's scary how well that works.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:56.580
I'm sure that even Polar Be—

00:07:57.990 --> 00:07:59.640
Oh, you're awake.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:01.300
Actually, I'm concentrating.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:02.040
Why?

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:04.360
Because when I take orders,

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:08.450
I feel like I need to listen to 
the customers very carefully.

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:10.010
You're a shining example 
of a café owner.

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:11.850
The way I see it,

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:14.650
I think you're trying 
too hard to fulfill

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:17.060
your job as the owner of the café.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:19.530
That's probably why you can't sleep.

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:22.190
But that's not what life's all about.

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:25.600
There are things you have to worry about and things you don't.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:27.480
As long as the pluses and minuses
 balance out to zero.

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:30.350
Hey! Don't fall asleep now!

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:32.300
I just said something important!

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:36.110
Oh, sorry.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:38.040
Why'd you wake us up?

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:39.700
Oh, that's right.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:43.300
Your hypnosis is amazing, Mr. Penguin.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:44.620
Yeah, that's not it.

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:48.850
Mr. Penguin, could I ask you a favor?

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:58.020
Penguin's 100 ways to 
manage your life.

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:01.980
Number 1: Understand that you 
have to compliment yourself.

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:05.800
Number 2: Be the last to put 
the blame on yourself.

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:11.070
Number 3: What you can't be done today, 
also can't be done tomorrow.

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:15.530
That was great, Mr. Penguin.

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:18.520
Great to hear, Mr. Polar Bear.

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:20.430
Must have worked really well.

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:23.410
So, what stuck in your mind the most.

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:25.000
Let's see...

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:28.960
Something about Penguin's 
Life or other.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:33.820
Huh? Isn't that the very beginning?

00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:36.790
Must have worked really well.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:42.970
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:41.730
Mr. Grizzly's First Love.

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:52.080
It's a complete snowscape.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:53.620
It's very pretty.

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:57.950
Hey! There wasn't a 
shovel in the shed!

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:00.770
It should have been resting against the side.

00:10:00.770 --> 00:10:04.530
What?! It's not inside the shed?

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:07.000
Aren't you going to 
hibernate, Mr. Grizzly?

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:09.280
Who the hell are the ones that keep

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:11.690
waking me up over and over?!

00:10:11.690 --> 00:10:14.430
Because of you guys, I'm wide awake.

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:17.590
Now it's going to take me forever 
to settle down to sleep.

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:20.230
I'm going to move around a bit!

00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:21.680
Let me snow shovel!

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.430
The shovel's by the shed, right?

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:26.440
Have fun.

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:32.750
You two seem to have completely 
different personalities,

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:34.300
but you get along so well.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:35.110
Totally.

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:40.750
Well, Grizzly and I are 
childhood friends.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.490
Are you two the same age?

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:47.320
Yup. We were in the same grade.

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:50.460
Snow, huh?

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:56.210
Days like this remind 
me of a lot of things.

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:19.610
I knew you'd be here.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:25.580
Oh, it's you, Polar Bear.

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:28.240
The teacher was looking for you.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.410
You've been summoned, haven't you?

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:36.040
I can't hibernate, so I'm tired.

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:37.720
So you're not going?

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:39.670
It's annoying.

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:41.760
They're just out to get me.

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:45.260
Well, you do stand out, Grizzly.

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:47.400
Must be nice to be you.

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:51.230
Liked by everyone, 
and an honor student.

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:53.220
You think so?

00:11:53.220 --> 00:11:54.590
I do.

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:59.080
Whatever. I guess I'll go.

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:01.070
That's probably a good idea.

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:04.420
Let's go home together.

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:05.690
Sure.

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:08.420
We'll meet up at the school gates.

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:09.390
Okay.

00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:17.210
So they were like...

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:21.540
"You act all big." 
So I told them,

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:24.930
"My voice and body are both 
big because of genetics!"

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:27.740
How much do you weigh now?

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:28.750
Two hundred kilograms.

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:30.010
What about you?

00:12:30.010 --> 00:12:31.640
Two twenty.

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:35.540
What the hell?! You're bigger than me!

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:38.250
Damn it. Why are they 
just out to get me...

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:42.170
Hey, Polar Bear.

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:48.530
So, well, um, uh...

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:50.750
I know.

00:12:51.260 --> 00:12:53.370
You're going there again today, right?

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:56.260
Y-Yeah...

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:09.180
Calm down.

00:13:11.510 --> 00:13:12.730
I-I am calm!

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:14.000
Really?

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:18.690
Aw man... school twice a 
week is totally enough.

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:18.690
Hell yeah! I'm so calm I'm 
about to fire it up!

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:20.980
Oh, here we go.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:24.440
A breeze.

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:28.640
You jerk!

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:31.280
Oh, here we go, for real.

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:34.270
That just seems too convenient.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:58.760
Oh, Miss Tsukiko is coming!

00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:00.230
You idiot!

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:04.330
Don't talk so loud!

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:06.320
All right, I'll talk more softly.

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:10.210
And?

00:14:10.210 --> 00:14:10.870
Huh?

00:14:12.640 --> 00:14:16.290
How does Miss Tsukiko 
seem to be to you?

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:19.710
How does she seem? Normal...

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:23.210
Normal?! That can't be right!

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:26.260
She's so elegant and graceful!

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:28.050
Whoa! She did a backflip.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:29.890
What?! Are you serious?!

00:14:30.860 --> 00:14:31.580
Just kidding.

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:34.160
You jerk!

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:46.240
You should at least talk to her.

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:48.740
It's not like that!

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:55.360
Let's stop by the book 
store on our way home.

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:56.730
S-Sure.

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:05.590
Damn that teacher!

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:09.310
He always talks too damn much!

00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:10.550
We're running pretty late...

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:14.490
If we miss the bus,
 I'm gonna beat his ass!

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:16.410
We're already twenty minutes late.

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:17.770
We're not going to make it.

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:32.160
What are you doing?

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:34.160
Quiet. Over there.

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:44.420
It looks like she's 
looking for something.

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:46.270
This is your chance.

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:46.800
Huh?

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:50.060
You can ask her if 
everything is okay and

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:51.350
then help her out.

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:52.760
Oh! I get it!

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:56.000
All right, it's up to you, Polar Bear.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:56.640
Huh?

00:15:57.770 --> 00:15:59.960
You should go, Grizzly.

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:01.610
This is your chance.

00:16:01.610 --> 00:16:03.360
It won't work if I go.

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:05.720
What? Why?

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:08.030
You already know.

00:16:08.930 --> 00:16:10.600
You know how I am.

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:13.250
On top of that, 
everyone is scared of me.

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:17.210
I don't want to scare Miss Tsukiko.

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:23.260
You're an honor student and no one's
 afraid of you, so you should go!

00:16:25.010 --> 00:16:26.870
I'll owe you for life, Polar Bear.

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:33.720
Hello.

00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:36.890
Is everything okay?

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:39.640
Huh? Well...

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:51.990
Man, she really is cute... 
she's always been cute.

00:17:10.270 --> 00:17:12.930
Polar Bear! What did Miss Tsukiko say?

00:17:14.530 --> 00:17:16.530
She said she lost her school badge.

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:17.890
School badge?

00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:21.140
This thing.

00:17:22.210 --> 00:17:24.180
Oh, that thing.

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:25.380
Grizzly.

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:27.060
What?

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:29.520
Let's take a little walk.

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:33.250
S-Sure...

00:17:34.660 --> 00:17:35.530
What?!

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:37.590
You're joking, right?

00:17:38.860 --> 00:17:42.370
It's one of your usual...

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:46.250
She said her family's moving.

00:17:47.680 --> 00:17:51.100
So that's why she was trying 
really hard to find it.

00:17:51.810 --> 00:17:53.500
Because it's a precious memory.

00:17:57.670 --> 00:17:58.840
I see...

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:06.480
She was really nice, 
and well-mannered.

00:18:07.590 --> 00:18:08.450
Yeah...

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:10.960
Her voice was really cute, too.

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:14.170
Yeah...

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:54.110
Did you say goodbye to 
all of your friends?

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:55.200
I did...

00:18:56.060 --> 00:18:57.120
Mom?

00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:58.450
What's the matter?

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:01.800
I'm going to try to find 
it one last time.

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:05.160
You can head on home.

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:07.880
Do you want me to look with you?

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:10.530
No, I'll be okay.

00:19:11.030 --> 00:19:14.080
Then make sure you get home 
before you catch a cold.

00:19:15.170 --> 00:19:15.910
Okay.

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:31.040
Miss Tsukiko.

00:19:32.710 --> 00:19:33.640
Eh?

00:19:34.890 --> 00:19:38.990
Is this what you were looking 
for, Miss Tsukiko?

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:50.750
Thank you very much.

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:56.650
Pardon me. By chance, 
are you Mr. Polar Bear

00:19:56.650 --> 00:19:58.520
whom I met the other day?

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:05.750
The snow's really 
starting to come down.

00:20:06.650 --> 00:20:10.560
I'll be fine, but you should 
head home, Miss Tsukiko.

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:13.070
But...

00:20:13.070 --> 00:20:14.220
It's fine.

00:20:14.930 --> 00:20:16.390
You should hurry.

00:20:18.490 --> 00:20:20.020
All right.

00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:25.470
Thank you very much, Mr. Polar Bear.

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:44.870
Take care.

00:20:54.260 --> 00:20:56.700
Even you'll catch a cold

00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:59.710
if you stay out in the 
snow too long, Grizzly.

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:06.030
I'm Grizzly. 
Like hell I'd catch a cold.

00:21:10.340 --> 00:21:12.540
But...

00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:18.050
Having something warm to drink 
doesn't sound like a bad idea.

00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:20.620
Sure.

00:21:21.810 --> 00:21:25.740
Then let's have some cocoa, 
with some marshmallows.

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:27.560
Yeah.

00:21:38.970 --> 00:21:40.680
So what happened after that?

00:21:40.680 --> 00:21:42.100
Nothing since.

00:21:42.670 --> 00:21:46.110
So that must have been 
Mr. Grizzly's first love.

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:50.430
Snow shoveling's done!

00:21:50.430 --> 00:21:53.120
Damn it, it's snowing again!

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:56.690
Do you want something warm to drink?

00:21:56.690 --> 00:21:59.420
Sounds good. Get me some cocoa.

00:22:02.750 --> 00:22:03.850
What about marshmallows?

00:22:04.950 --> 00:22:06.380
Damn straight.

00:22:07.390 --> 00:22:09.970
You two get along so well.

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:11.390
That's so nice.

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:12.740
Yeah, so nice.

00:22:14.380 --> 00:22:17.860
What? You guys are acting weird.

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:24.760
Next Time

00:23:58.230 --> 00:23:59.880
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.880 --> 00:24:01.370
What is it, Panda?

00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:03.060
If you were going to 
be a live sacrifice,

00:24:03.060 --> 00:24:04.550
how would you like it to be done?

00:24:04.550 --> 00:24:06.250
Apparently there are a lot of

00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:08.360
questions left in this world 
that I don't want to answer.

00:24:08.360 --> 00:24:09.550
Please end this, Panda.

00:24:09.550 --> 00:24:10.630
Let's see...

00:24:10.630 --> 00:24:13.050
Let's get it straight 
already, Miss Sasako.

00:24:13.050 --> 00:24:14.470
That's my line.

00:24:14.470 --> 00:24:16.260
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:18.130
Next week's Polar Bear's Café,

00:24:18.130 --> 00:24:19.970
will be dedicated especially to you.

00:24:19.970 --> 00:24:22.310
Why are you suddenly talking
 like some popular Korean actor?

00:24:21.500 --> 00:24:25.450
Pun Café
The Secret to Delicious Coffee
Mr. Full-Time Panda, Mr. Llama and Rin Rin

00:24:22.310 --> 00:24:23.450
Enjoy!
